    {
      "key": "t0d588db51bcab333",
      "english": "<span data-i18n-slot=\"0\">Gold is traditionally considered a store of value. During uncertain economic or geopolitical conditions, some investors increase their exposure to gold, which may increase demand and support its price. However, gold prices can also decline depending on broader market conditions.</span>",
      "kind": "html",
      "sources": [
        "CMS:blogs/what-factors-influence-gold-and-silver-prices-in-the-global-market#content",
        "SSR:/blogs/what-factors-influence-gold-and-silver-prices-in-the-global-market"
      ],
      "translation": "<span data-i18n-slot=\"0\">金は伝統的に価値を保存するものと考えられています。経済状況や地政学的状況が不確実な場合、一部の投資家は金へのエクスポージャーを増やし、それが需要を増加させ、金の価格を支える可能性があります。ただし、より広範な市場状況によっては、金価格が下落する可能性もあります。</span>"
    },
